while working; short messages in the originating conversation.\\n- L19–L20: few concepts / few settings — new business need becomes an attribute of an existing concept or prompt text, not a new concept or setting.\\n\\n## S3 deepseek_intake.json (src/core/intake.ts, 1–63) — the flow\\n- source_sha256 `323aadefea69436ba23ed2de3bdbaad673d61915be9e239f3233ecf551a74179`; packet sha256 `d794df820efd11166ef801d30e287a923c16c35dc9e666484be4fad6fdc9bf97`\\n- L1, L11–14: module = trigger ingestion, thread correlation, subscription fan-out, eval queuing.\\n- L21: timestamp normalization to canonical ISO before anything else.\\n- L22: invariant — a trigger must belong to >=1 thread (throws).\\n- L23: idempotency by trigger id -> `'duplicate'`.\\n- L25–29: gate is `this.options.scope.scope(trigger)`; not listened -> persist trigger AND a `filtered` disposition with reason code + empty fanout -> `'filtered'`. Note: filtered triggers are still stored (auditability) but never fanned out or evaluated.\\n- L31, L37: thread correlation is symmetric union of co-occurring thread keys (`thread.correlated`) — derived, not configured.\\n- L38: fan-out iterates `thread.subscriptions` — subscriptions are per-thread and drive delivery (\\\"subscription pass-through\\\").\\n- L42–44: `followed` (thread-level context subscription) + `resumes = trigger.human && ticket.ended?.by !== 'human' && !followed`; ended tickets are skipped unless a human message resumes them; a human-stopped ticket receives nothing (mandate withdrawn).\\n- L45, L51: context-subscription tickets get inputs flagged `context: true` — the worker is told this is ambient context, not a direct ask. Precedence rule: any non-context (own) thread reach flips context false.\\n- L49–52: input ids are deterministic (`key('input', ticketId, 'trigger', trigger.id)`) — replay-safe fan-out.\\n- L53–55: disposition record {fanout, context?, at} persisted per trigger.\\n- L58: only if `this.owners(trigger).length === 0` is the trigger queued for Eval — unclaimed human messages and every bot message get a fallback owner; claimed ones do not.\\n- L59: wake each fanned-out ticket after persistence.\\n- L60: emits `trigger.received` for observers.\\n- Ordering: normalize -> validate -> dedupe -> filter -> save -> correlate -> fan out -> disposition -> eval fallback -> wake -> emit. Pure function of persisted state up to `this.now()` and `scope.scope`.\\n\\n## Prototype vs architecture article vs unimplemented\\n- Public prototype (implemented, inspected text): S3 pipeline above; README S1 L7 one-repo GitHub(+optional Feishu) scope; record-only mode for unrequested work per S2 L11.\\n- Architecture article (*Exploring Super-agent Design*): referenced only by title in S1 L5; its content is NOT in the supplied materials. Anything attributed to it here is a direction, not verified behavior.\\n- Explicitly unimplemented / not evidenced: per S1 L5 \\\"some designs ... are not implemented in this prototype\\\"; the materials never enumerate which. No multi-repo, no autonomous-initiation path beyond written rules, no evidence of cross-repository or multi-agent topologies. Also no code paths for `followupOwners`, `queueForEval`, `scope`, `Tickets.addInput`, `EnginePart` — only call sites; their internals are unevidenced.\\n- Non-claim: no execution, build, or test was run; all statements are source-text inspection only.\\n\",\"path\":\"work/quest_34771f670396/source_extraction.md\"}", "name": "file_write"}, "id": "call_00_NOW2WJeHWYv2LtqplgMi0231", "type": "function"}]}
